<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Naspers H1 shr up pre-abnormals.</title>
<headline>Naspers H1 shr up pre-abnormals.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     54	    vs 83</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   43	    vs 34</p>
<p>    Shr, &quot;N&quot; shares (cts) 55	    vs 39</p>
<p>    Attrib		    60.50	 vs 92.37</p>
<p>    Net, pre-abnormals    48.10	 vs 38.54</p>
<p>    Abnormal items paid    0.51	 vs received 48.86</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   84.05	 vs 63.26</p>
<p>    Tax			 35.95	 vs 24.72</p>
<p>    Interest received     15.63	 vs  8.19</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    4.83	 vs  0.79</p>
<p>    Turnover		 808.47	 vs 667.34</p>
<p>    Share of associates'   12.79	vs  5.91</p>
<p>Full name: Nasionale Pers Beperk</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that its publications expected to receive increased advertising revenue over the Christmas period. But expectations for the year as a whole were not high given unstable trading conditions, high interest rates and the tardiness of education authorities in getting into gear. Some had decided not to order textbooks for next year.</p>
<p>The group traditionally does not declare an interim dividend.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
